aarch64 #23 milestone-4 probe: own task_self in-guest (mint).

Mints the task-self port in-guest (overriding the 0055 seed) when CIDER_INGUEST_IPC is on. For the
self-contained case task_self is now only the self-VM short-circuit target (compared against this same
minted value) with 0 ciderd deallocate/mod_refs, so a guest-minted name fully replaces the seeded real
name -- a positive signal that the guest can own its task port space (the milestone-4 gate to removing
checkin). exec-true RECV 19 -> 18 (task_self_trap 1 -> 0), rc=0, soak 10/10. Flag-off unchanged. fork
resets _cached_task_self so the child re-mints. On top of 0057.

diff --git a/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/src/xnu_syscall/mach/impl/mach_traps.c b/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/src/xnu_syscall/mach/impl/mach_traps.c
